ut in um yeah so the  first thing i do whenever like when i  get on the plane or whatever i'm  watching i'm gonna watch the opponent  i'm gonna see where they top runs top  passes their formations and then after i  feel like i got a comfortable  comfortable read of what they do  now i'm studying runners you know i need  to know their fumble history i need to  know what the what ball they love to  create their hands i'm gonna carry the  ball in because a lot of people don't  teach them body ball boundary put the  ball on the outside so you know i'm  trying to watch over that and then  seeing when guys go through traffic how  are they carrying the ball if they're  going to try to put four points of  pressure on it or not so my eyes are  automatically 24 7 on the ball so every  chance i get you know trying to get a  good clean punch out on it you guys have  won three of the last four now carson  wins trying to put together this second  chapter if you will of his career in  indianapolis how has he impacted this  locker room man he impacted a lot man  and you know i'm loving everything that  he's doing you know he's been a great  leader great teammate and he's doing a  great job by shutting the damn daughters  up you don't think he's doing anybody  get talking trash about who he is and  you know what he did in philly but  people got to understand that you know  this is the next chapter in his life and  he's stepping up in every big every way  that he possibly can and i just pray  that he continue to get better continue  to lead his offense obviously quentin  nelson he's not a hundred percent but  just talk to us about how important it  is to have him back on the field  especially with that running back that  you got back there i mean whenever cue  nelly out there man you know that's  always great for our offense and you  know they're going to run the ball  behind them and you're going to make  sure that he's helping everybody out  whenever he gets a chance in the pass  game so that's one thing about q man  he's a nasty guy you know he want to get  down he want to get dirty so when having  him back man that's that's that  mentality that mean mentality that we  need on office line i got to ask you  this because it just popped in my mind  when i was out there right there  watching xavier rhodes warm up the dude  was limping  he was limping and he still went out  there he fought and clawed came up with  a key interception man that was big um  because um like you said in warm-ups  like he said he did one thing in  warm-ups and then aggravated his calf  and so he went right into the locker  room so he was kind of scared to see if  he was going to play or not but he  stepped up big whenever we needed to so  that's one thing about having a veteran  cornerback in this league you know he's  been great for us so that play was very  big to get us off the field get the  offense back run some time off the clock  and we scored there so that was  definitely a great big play by him well  we've been traveling around all fall we  did do these post-game interviews  electric we've seen some unbelievable  chains that's got to be the coolest  chain we've seen the entire year talk me  through the process behind this one hey  man you got to be rich  i got to give it to my wife i went i  went home i went home friday yeah she  said i got a surprise for you she said  all the hard work that you've done you  know everything that you do in the game  you you're always focused you're always  weird by somebody else and she just  wanted to kind of show a little token of  her love for me so you know i just got  to thank my baby for this one that's  awesome and your daughter too i heard  you've been dancing with her a little  bit we even got the video right here yes  sir man you know my daughter's a mean to  me uh well especially my oldest one  she she's got a minnie mouse because  she's a better dancer that's true that  is true she's like she's a goofball man  i love